# `ys::pprint` - The YS Pretty Printing Library

The `ys::pprint` library formats Clojure data consistently across the JVM,
Babashka, Jolt, and Glojure runtimes.
Its default right margin is 72 columns and its default miser width is 40.

```yaml
use pprint: :all
```

```mdys:fmt-fns
pp(X) nil: Pretty print a value to the current output stream
write(X Opt*) Str|nil: Pretty print a value with Clojure pprint options
```

Pass `:stream nil` to `write` to return the formatted string.
The `:right-margin`, `:miser-width`, `:length`, `:level`, `:pretty`,
`:stream`, and `:suppress-namespaces` options are supported.

The always available `pp` function in `ys::std` delegates to
`ys::pprint/pp`.
It remains available for convenience, while `use pprint:` provides explicit
access to the library.
